Feature: slice-6 / notification-svc-i18n-templates
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-6
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §14.7 ("transactional emails in PL + EN with per-event templates")

What was built
==============
Two new transactional-email events get the same per-locale template
+ RPC treatment that `invitation` already had:

  - email_verification — sent by identity-svc after self-serve signup
                         to deliver the Firebase Auth verification link
                         under our own branding.
  - quota_warning      — sent by billing-svc when an org crosses 80%
                         or 95% of its monthly token quota for the
                         first time in the period.

For each event the four artifacts ship together:

  proto/notification/v1/notification.proto
    + SendEmailVerification RPC + SendEmailVerificationRequest
      (recipient_email, first_name, verify_url, expires_at_iso, locale)
    + SendQuotaWarning RPC + SendQuotaWarningRequest
      (recipient_email, first_name, organization_name, usage_percent,
       tokens_remaining, plan_tier, plan_cycle, period_end_iso,
       billing_url, locale)

  services/notification-svc/internal/i18n/templates/pl/email_verification.md
  services/notification-svc/internal/i18n/templates/en/email_verification.md
  services/notification-svc/internal/i18n/templates/pl/quota_warning.md
  services/notification-svc/internal/i18n/templates/en/quota_warning.md
    YAML frontmatter (subject) + body with {placeholder} markers
    matching the proto request fields.

  services/notification-svc/internal/adapters/grpc/invitation_email.go
    + SendEmailVerification handler — InvalidArgument gates,
      template Load with locale fallback to PL, Render with the
      proto field map, dispatch via existing s.emailer.
    + SendQuotaWarning handler — same shape, plus a 1..100 sanity
      check on usage_percent so a malformed call doesn't render
      "0%" or "1000%".
    + firstNameOrDefault helper — drops a literal "Hi ," when the
      caller doesn't know the recipient's first name. Locale-aware
      ("there" for EN, empty for PL where the comma-after-name
      pattern reads cleaner blank).

Why these two events + this scope
==================================
docs/18 §14.7 named the three transactional emails the web app needs
for launch: invitation (already shipped Slice 1 commit 7), email
verification, and quota warning. Push-only notifications stay
out-of-band — this work is only about the emails.

The RPCs are added but not yet wired from the upstream services. Per
the established pattern (the invitation RPC shipped before identity-
svc started calling it from InviteTherapist), the wiring lands in a
follow-up commit on each caller:

  - identity-svc.RegisterTherapist / RegisterOrganization →
    SendEmailVerification (needs Firebase Admin's
    GenerateEmailVerificationLink first).
  - billing-svc.CommitUsage → SendQuotaWarning (needs the
    per-period "warned_at_80 / warned_at_95" idempotency flag added
    to subscriptions or organization_quota).

Both follow-ups are tracked in PROGRESS.md.

How verified
============
1. buf generate proto → clean.
   Generated Go now exports SendEmailVerification + SendQuotaWarning
   on NotificationServiceClient + Server interfaces.

2. go build ./... across the workspace → exit 0 on
   gen/go, services/notification-svc, services/identity-svc,
   services/billing-svc, services/clinical-svc.

3. go test ./internal/i18n/... → 7/7 pass (new file
   templater_test.go):
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/pl/invitation
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/pl/email_verification
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/pl/quota_warning
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/en/invitation
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/en/email_verification
     TestLoad_AllTemplates_BothLocales/en/quota_warning
     TestLoad_UnknownLocaleFallsBackToPL

   The first six explicitly assert that EVERY {placeholder} in the
   proto's request type is substituted by Render. If a future
   template typos a key (e.g. "{first_nname}"), the corresponding
   subtest fails with "placeholder {first_name} not substituted".

4. The two new templates parse the same frontmatter format as the
   shipping `invitation.md` — same i18n.Load codepath, same renderer.
   No engine changes were needed.

